      "message": "Regarding the comment http://b/280450222#comment3, is this how the per-app driver selection going to work:\n\n1. when `persist.graphics.egl` is `ANGLE`:\n\n\"default\": use ANGLE binary in /vendor.\n\"angle\": use ANGLE apk if there is one. what to do if there is no ANGLE apk? \n\"native\": use ANGLE binary in /vendor. (EGL Loader.cpp will load `persist.graphics.egl` first before `ro.hardware.egl`)\n\n2. when `persist.graphics.egl` is native GLES driver name:\n\n\"default\": use native GLES driver binary in /vendor.\n\"angle\": use ANGLE apk is there is one. what to do if there is no ANGLE apk?\n\"native\": use native GLES driver binary in /vendor.\n\nIf above is the intended new behavior. What is the plan if per-app switch is set to use \"angle\" but the ANGLE apk is not available?",
